a deadly and unprovoked attack on a  local beach that left one person dead  and another with permanent damage has  stymied police now for a decade yeah two  people were attacked at six mile cove on  lake mojave by a muscular killer with a  bad temper cold case detectives believe  it's a mystery that can still be solved  though the i-team's george knapp has our  story  the sign leading the six-mile cove  proved prophetic for two las vegas out  for a day at the beach on lake mojave a  few miles east of searchlight the cove  is a bit out of the way known mostly to  locals and to windsurfers leo cardenas  and his girlfriend rosa castrohone drove  from las vegas to try out leo's new  metal detector on october 24 2011 a time  of year when few campers used the beach  as leo and rosa scoured the sand they  came closer to a lone camper on the  south side of the beach and something  set him off as they got a little bit  closer to where he was camping along the  shoreline  of the lake  he  walked up on him and shot both of them  killing one right there and  seriously wounding and paralyzing the  other victim rosa was shot in the head  and died on the spot leo somehow got  back on his feet and was shot again but  was still alive detectives say the  suspect walked back to his truck grabbed  the knife and returned to stab cardenas  multiple times amazingly he was still  alive and survived a long terrible night  lying next to the body of his loved one  the next morning a visitor to the beach  came across the carnage and called  authorities metro's cold case team say  the attack was unprovoked totally  innocent not engaged in any risky  behavior whatsoever not engaged in any  aggressive behavior  all accounts they were pretty humble  docile hard-working people and they were  out there minding their own business  cardenas survived but lost the use of  his legs he's since moved to mexico  detectives don't know if the attack was  a hate crime unleashed on victims who  were both hispanic this was the  description of the killer as of 2011 he  was large over six feet tall and 200  pounds muscle bound in his late 40s to  early 50s they speculate he might be a  loner with a short fuse and a violent  past who's familiar with the area his  vehicle at the time was a tan or gold  jeep cherokee at the scene police  collected tire tracks boot prints and  dna but they have yet to find a match in  any dna database this case is solvable  they say what's needed is either a  future dna match or for someone in the  public to focus on the clues and make  the connection to an angry loner who  looked like this ten years ago somebody  might see the composite the artist's  rendition of the suspect couple that  with the vehicle type and description  and in 2011 at that location and give us  a call you know if you're wrong we'll  figure it out george knapp 8 news now  homicide detectives say that access to  dna databases is useful in helping to  solve cold case mysteries but because of  privacy concerns dna information is  often off limits for police agencies
 

